Derived components, with their upstream sources:

  windows/audio_format.cpp, windows/audio_format.h
      packages/system_audio_capture/windows/system_audio_capture_plugin.cpp
      (mix-format detection for IEEE float and integer PCM, the interleaved
       mono down-mix including 24-bit sign extension and unsigned-8 centering,
       and the phase-continuous linear resampler with its rationale)

  windows/capture_session.cpp
      packages/system_audio_capture/windows/system_audio_capture_plugin.cpp
      (the WASAPI shared-mode loopback initialisation sequence, reading the
       endpoint mix format rather than assuming it, the 200 ms buffer request,
       the MMCSS "Pro Audio" registration, the poll cadence of half the buffer
       clamped to 5-100 ms and split into 5 ms slices for bounded stop latency,
       and the AUDCLNT_BUFFERFLAGS_SILENT zero-fill)

  windows/audio_flutter_windows_plugin.cpp
      packages/system_audio_capture/windows/system_audio_capture_plugin.cpp
      (render endpoint enumeration with PKEY_Device_FriendlyName, and the
       platform-thread task queue drained from a top-level window proc)

  windows/CMakeLists.txt
      packages/system_audio_capture/windows/CMakeLists.txt
      (plugin target layout, NOMINMAX, and the link set)

The Windows SDK header-ordering hazard documented in these files was also first
recorded upstream.

The pull-model session lifecycle, the bounded frame ring and its drop
accounting, the stall watchdog, the COM RAII wrappers, the playback render path,
and the entire Dart layer are original to this package.
